        "anchor": [
          0,
          3962.5,
          "lt"
        ]
      },
      "text": "A step can read and compute at the same time, so it takes as long as the slower of the two. The ridge,\n1.27 T ÷ 48.6 G = 26.2 FLOP per byte, splits the chart: decode at 0.5 sits far down the memory slope, while\nprefill of the same 870 tokens, at 200.8, sits under the roof and reaches 0.99 TFLOP/s on the same weights.",
      "originalText": "A step can read and compute at the same time, so it takes as long as the slower of the two. The ridge,\n1.27 T ÷ 48.6 G = 26.2 FLOP per byte, splits the chart: decode at 0.5 sits far down the memory slope, while\nprefill of the same 870 tokens, at 200.8, sits under the roof and reaches 0.99 TFLOP/s on the same weights.",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
