      "customData": {
        "section": "5-sweep",
        "anchor": [
          0,
          6973.5,
          "lt"
        ]
      },
      "text": "B = 64 sits at 29.4 FLOP per byte, just past the ridge: 26.2, or 27.1 with this run's own 48.3 GB/s and\n1.31 TFLOP/s. The jump at 16 is what we saw; a different MPS matmul kernel taking over is likely, but unproven",
      "originalText": "B = 64 sits at 29.4 FLOP per byte, just past the ridge: 26.2, or 27.1 with this run's own 48.3 GB/s and\n1.31 TFLOP/s. The jump at 16 is what we saw; a different MPS matmul kernel taking over is likely, but unproven",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b3t"
    },
